[h2]Build 0.9.50[/h2]
[h3]Changed[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Fuel bill:[/b] the burner's Fuels menu is now a [b]Fuel bill[/b], laid out like a vanilla bill. Set a [b]fuel search radius[/b] so colonists only fetch fuel from nearby, and pick fuels in the full filter tree - with its search box, categories and special filters such as fresh or rotten corpses. [b]Anything[/b] and [b]Trashbricks only[/b] buttons, and each fuel's value and exhaust listed alongside. Hoppers follow the filter too. Your existing fuel choices carry over.
[*][b]Corpses are worth their mass:[/b] a trashbrick is compressed matter, so it takes 5 kg of corpse to match 1 kg of brick. A human corpse is now worth about 13 bricks (was 1.5), a muffalo about 30. Corpses still burn with a huge cloud of rot stink.
[/list]
